      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chronic pelvic pain is one of the most difficult conditions encountered by health professionals working with women both in primary and secondary care. The cause is variable, and for some women a diagnosis is never determined. While it is acknowledged that it is a symptom and not a condition, many women and professionals continue to seek a cause and cure. It is contended that this client group is best supported by a multidisciplinary approach to symptom control that incorporates the skills of the gynaecologist, physiotherapist, nurse, psychologist and pain management specialist. This is often difficult to achieve within a resource-limited environment. An alternative approach is suggested using current resources, which provides patient education and support, thus empowering women to influence their health behaviours and situations."},
